A template literal is a string enclosed by backticks (``) that can span
multiple lines and can include a JavaScript expression in curly braces,
prefixed with a dollar sign (${expression}). Template literals are great
when we need to merge static text with variables.
A tagged template literal is a template string that is executed through a
function that is specified immediately before the template literal string.
The function is executed on the template literal before the string is
rendered in the browser.
So, Emotion's css function is being used in a tagged template literal to render the
styles defined in backticks (``) on the HTML element.
