Let's examine some key points in this class:
RequestDelegate represents the reference to the next element in the pipeline.
This could be a delegate or other class-based middleware.
InvokeAsync is the core part of our middleware. This contains the
implementation of the middleware and calls the _next element in our pipeline.
At this point, our implementation must choose between continuing the pipeline
or only returning a result to the client. For example, in the case of a not authorized
message, the middleware will interrupt the pipeline.
